| Build - tokenise the BASIC sources in src, next to this file.
|
| Copy to RISC OS as an Obey file (type &FEB), with BuildIn.exec as &FFF beside
| it, and double-click it. The sources are plain text; LIBRARY and LOAD both
| need tokenised files, so they have to be converted once on this side.
| *BASIC -load tokenises a textual program on the way in and stops in immediate
| mode, which is what lets BuildIn drive it.
|
| -load rather than -quit: -quit runs a CRUNCH %1111 over the program, which
| strips the spaces and REMs these sources are largely made of.
|
| The SAVE and QUIT reach BASIC through { < ... }, which redirects the input of
| ONE command. *Exec would set the input stream globally and is not consumed at
| all when the command arrives over a HostCmd socket, so an Exec-driven build
| silently does nothing headless -- it needs a real keyboard. Redirection works
| both ways round, so this builds from a double-click and from a script.
|
| BuildIn is shared by all five, with the destination in Build$Target: FileSwitch
| expands <Build$Target> when BASIC resolves the path SAVE hands it.
Set Build$Dir <Obey$Dir>
Set Build$Target PatLib
BASIC -load <Build$Dir>.src.PatLib { < <Build$Dir>.BuildIn }
Set Build$Target TestPat
BASIC -load <Build$Dir>.src.TestPat { < <Build$Dir>.BuildIn }
Set Build$Target ModeServ
BASIC -load <Build$Dir>.src.ModeServ { < <Build$Dir>.BuildIn }
Set Build$Target ModeTest
BASIC -load <Build$Dir>.src.ModeTest { < <Build$Dir>.BuildIn }
Set Build$Target ModeSweep
BASIC -load <Build$Dir>.src.ModeSweep { < <Build$Dir>.BuildIn }
Unset Build$Target
